      "file": "/workspace/generated_images/exec-a8b85e76-ca72-431d-b041-1feb8ebde0f5.png",
      "prompt": "Create a NEW pixel-art game base animation atlas of TAILS PILOTING THE CYCLONE WALKER from SONIC ADVENTURE2, matching the attached new32pose machine/pilot reference exactly. FOUR COLUMNS by FOUR ROWS, exactly16 genuine distinct complete drawings, SQUARE transparentRGBA canvas. No grid, text, labels, background, extra characters, no aircraft wings, no four wheels. Every cell includes the ENTIRE blue/yellow two-legged Cyclone and Tails visible at the open cockpit controls, both mechanicalfeet and tailtips fully contained. Character+machine only central55%width and65%height; leave generous transparent padding on every edge. Two mechanicallegs, compact roundedbluebody/yellowpanels, built-in frontVulcan cannon and chassis missilebox, jointedgraylegs and broad blue/yellow feet. Tails orangefur, blueeyes, whitemuzzle/twintailtips, whitegloves, three foreheadtufts. No emptyrobot, no handheld gun, no redTornado plane or Eggmanwalker. Facing screenRIGHT consistently.\nRow1 IDLE: bothfeet planted and Tails watchesright; leans over controls; looks up as twins tails lift; returns alert at controls. Four visibly different pilot/legbodygestures, not recolors.\nRow2 RUN/WALK: actual TWO-LEGGED mechanical locomotion cycle, rightleg stepsforward; weight passes over plantedrightfoot and leftleg lifts; leftleg stepsforward; kneescompressandrightlegbeginsto lift. Tails stays seated/piloting, bothlegs and entiremachine visible in everycell. No wheels or floatingjet flight.\nRow3 ATTACK VULCAN CANNON: Tails grips controls and chassis braces; frontVulcancannon turns slightlyright; small compact YELLOW bullet muzzle flash from built-infrontbarrel with machine recoil; barrel settles and legs restoreguard. Keep wholemachine clearlyvisible, no enormous laserbeam and no attack fromfoxhands.\nRow4 HIT/RECOVERY: walker torso recoils backwards slightly, kneesbend; Tails ducks overcontrols and machine plantsonefoot; machineleanslowcatchingbalance; returns to stablealertstance. Four different poses, no destruction, no gore, no new damage mechanic.\nThis is adapted game choreography, not a claim of official frame-by-frame source sprites.",
